adr: 0217
file: lib/dialect/pasjson.pas
kills: lib_json
why: RFC 8259 §2 makes a document one value. Two messages arriving in one buffer is the ordinary case for a client that frames by Content-Length and gets the framing wrong, and answering the first value hides that from the one code that could notice -- the parse succeeds, the second message is dropped, and the stream is out of step from then on with nothing to point at. This is also what makes the leading-zero refusal beside it redundant, so it is the check that carries both.
--- old
    SkipWhite(b, at);
    if not AtEnd(b, at) then begin
      JsonFree(v);
      e := errSyntax
    end
--- new
    SkipWhite(b, at)
